   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re on Route 4 — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: SOUTH → Route 3 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; EAST → Cerulean City — a Mart, a Pokémon Center. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 24; an unfamiliar area; Route 2. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been.. Okay — to get past this I need the S.S. Ticket — a guy named Bill, in the house past the Nugget Bridge to the north, hands it over.. You keep trying to travel:3,21 but the world hasn\'t changed in 4 turns - it went \'travel:no_path\', and you don\'t seem to be getting anywhere.. That one stung — that trainer (their lead was zubat, poison/flying-type and they had a full team) at Route 24 just put you down. Be honest about WHY before you charge back in: their poison/flying lead may have the type edge on you. The fix here isn\'t trying again harder, it\'s coming back stronger — leveling up or grabbing a teammate for backup and type coverage is the real play. You CAN retry once if you\'re feeling it, but going in unchanged ends the same way. (Your call.). ekans, spearow and rattata are too weak for those trainers (zubat lead, a full team) at Route 24 — so before I push through, I\'m going to level the weak ones up to about L16 (field THEM in the grass, not my strongest — that\'s how the whole team gets stronger). Then I go back and cross. (My call — but charging in under-levelled just blacks me out again.). HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 2 of 8 — next is Misty in Cerulean City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an abra around Route 24 / Route 25. It grows into my alakazam — that\'s my answer for Erika AND Koga down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "The people here were robbed. It\'s obvious that TEAM ROCKET is behind this most heinous crime! Even our POLICE FORCE has trouble with the ROCKETS!"; "What? I\'m waiting for my friends to find me here."; "POK. BALL, and you want 1. That will be .200. Okay?"; "POK. BALL? Certainly. How many would you like?". YOUR PLAN — right now: Level the weak ones (ekans, spearow and rattata) to ~L16 by fielding THEM in the grass, THEN retry. Next: Build a team strong enough to beat a trainer at Route 24, then push on toward Cerulean City. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L24), ekans (L11), spearow (L11), rattata (L10). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "1 badge(s) earned (Boulder). Next gym: Misty of Cerulean City. Pokédex: 5 caught. She's one badge in — the adventure's really starting (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L24), ekans (L11), spearow (L11), rattata (L10)', 'goal': {'short': 'Level the weak ones (ekans, spearow and rattata) to ~L16 by fielding THEM in the grass, THEN retry', 'medium': 'Build a team strong enough to beat a trainer at Route 24, then push on toward Cerulean City', 'long': 'Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge'}} options=['head_to_gym', 'battle', 'wander_catch', 'travel:3,21', 'travel:3,43', 'travel:3,27', 'travel:3,20', 'travel:3,26', 'fetch_keeper']

