en you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 2 of 8 — next is Misty in Cerulean City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an abra around Route 24 / Route 25. It grows into my alakazam — that\'s my answer for Erika AND Koga down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "The people here were robbed. It\'s obvious that TEAM ROCKET is behind this most heinous crime! Even our POLICE FORCE has trouble with the ROCKETS!"; "What? I\'m waiting for my friends to find me here."; "POK. BALL, and you want 1. That will be .200. Okay?"; "POK. BALL? Certainly